# Repo Scope & Structure (NX monorepo)

- This is an NX monorepo with deployables under `apps/` and shared libraries under `libs/`.
- Backend services live under: `apps/backend/<domain>/<service-name>/`
  Example (Identity): `apps/backend/identity/auth-service/` (preferred)
- Do NOT place new backend services directly under `apps/` root unless the repo already does so.
- Shared cross-service contracts live under `libs/contracts/*`.
- Shared utilities (auth guard, logging, validation) live under `libs/shared/*`.

When creating a new service:

1. Create folder in the correct domain path.
2. Add service README and SERVICE_SPEC.md.
3. Add Dockerfile + test setup + Swagger.
4. Ensure it can run locally via docker compose.

Never break the structure defined in docs/architecture/decisions.md and docs/architecture/domains.md.
